# R6-2 (1), task (2): a reference field of a merge result body, read by the common body construction -- `@: Model p` is
# the typed reference cell holding nothing, as a named Structure's is (unit_null_struct_deref_catch's Holder); the
# result's copy holds nothing too, and a field read through it is the implicit `interpreter` throw, taken by
# `catch: interpreter ()` (Codex CODEX-STRUCT-NULL-20261011-151401).  The merge stands in a method, so the body is read
# where the method stands.  Exit 7 through the catch; 81 when the read went through, 82 when k came back wrong.
Model:
    int: v 11
end: Model

fn: m () int
    R: merge: Model
        @: Model p
        int: k 3
    end: merge
    int: got 81
    ---
        got: R\p\v
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 7
    if: R\k != 3
        got: 82
    return: got
end: m

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
